<title>USA: Vermont House might weight powerball lottery bill.</title>
<headline>Vermont House might weight powerball lottery bill.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>As the Vermont legislature approaches the end of its 1997 session, lawmakers are facing a flurry of proposed legislation, with major issues, such as the budget and school funding, still remain unresolved.</p>
<p>But the House and Senate are clearing the books of other issues, including a proposal for the state to join the Powerball Lottery game.</p>
<p>But even if the measure passes the House, it still has to go to the Senate and the governor. And Gov. Howard Dean has been an outspoken critic of expanding lottery games.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
